    },
    "name": {
      "value": "Greater Desolation Locket"
    },
    "source": {
      "value": "tv"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "The surface of this golden, heart-shaped locket is nearly worn through with cracks. If opened, it reveals a portrait of someone the bearer loved dearly and has lost. The spell DC of any spell cast by activating this item is 24. The desolation locket numbs you to further despair, and you gain a +2 item bonus to saving throws against emotion effects. (emotion, mental) After you cast an enchantment spell by activating the locket, you emanate an aura of hopelessness in a 5-foot emanation until the start of your next turn. A creature that ends its turn in the aura must succeed at a Will saving throw against the locket's spell DC or become slowed 1 (slowed 2 on a critical failure) until the end of its next turn. You cast haunting hymn. The item bonus when affixed to armor is +3, and the spell DC is 30. You cast 4th-level agonizing despair. You cast crushing despair."
    },
